<Routines>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The following three rungs reverse the bytes in each element of an array.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung initializes the tags for subsequent rungs:

The CLR instruction clears index. The next rungs uses index to act on a different element in the array.

The SIZE instruction finds the number of elements in array and stores that value in array_length. A subsequent rung uses this value to determine when the routine has acted on all the elements in the array.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(index)SIZE(array[0],0,array_length);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung reverses the bytes in one element of array.

The SWPB instruction reverses the bytes of the element number that is indicated by the value of index. For example, when index equals 0, the SWPB instruction acts on array[0].

The ADD instruction increments index. The next time the rung executes, the SWPB instruction will act on the next element in array..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(swap_bytes)SWPB(array[index],REVERSE,array_bytes_reverse[index])ADD(1,index,index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung determines when the SWPB instruction has acted on all the elements in the array.

If index is less then the number of elements in the array (array_length), then execution jumps to the rung that has the swap_bytes label (the previous rung). This lets the routine act on the next element in the array.

If index equals the number of elements in the array (array_length), then the SWPB has acted on all the elements in the array. Execution goes to the next rung.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LES(index,array_length)JMP(swap_bytes);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
